+++ b/README.md
@@ -14,3 +14,10 @@ Prices are integer cents everywhere. Run the tests with `npm test`.
 more. An unknown code, or one the order does not qualify for, is refused with an error and the order is unchanged.
 `totals` shows the discount as `discountCents`; it never touches shipping, and free shipping is decided on the items
 before any discount.
+
+## Monthly export
+
+`orders.exportMonth('YYYY-MM')` returns CSV text for the accountant: a header line, then one line per order placed in
+that month, by number. Columns: `order`, `date` (as stored), `customer`, `email`, `phone`, `total` (what the customer
+pays, discount and shipping included, in euros with two decimals). Values with a comma or a quote are quoted. A month
+without orders gives the header alone; a month not written `YYYY-MM` throws a `RangeError`.
